<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="GBrowser: Bookmarks and history" id="GBrowser-Bookmarks-and-History">

    <primary-label ref="gbrowser"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Bookmark the page: <shortcut>Ctrl+D</shortcut></p>
        <p>Bookmark Manager: <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+B</shortcut></p>
        <p>Stored per project in <path>.idea/gbrowsers.xml</path></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Bookmark pages in GBrowser, open them from the bookmarks bar or the Bookmarks menu, edit them, and clear history and cookies.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Bookmark pages, use the bookmarks bar, and clear history and cookies.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Manage GBrowser bookmarks and browsing history in JetBrains IDEs: bookmark pages, use the bookmarks bar, edit bookmarks, clear history and cookies.</web-summary>

    <p>
        GBrowser keeps bookmarks and a short browsing history for each project.
        Both are stored with the GBrowser settings in <path>.idea/gbrowsers.xml</path>.
    </p>
    <p>
        The default shortcuts in this topic are for Windows and Linux.
        On macOS, GBrowser shortcuts use <shortcut>⌘</shortcut> instead of <shortcut>Ctrl</shortcut> and <shortcut>⌥</shortcut> instead of <shortcut>Alt</shortcut>; see <a href="GBrowser-Keyboard-Shortcuts.topic" anchor="macos-shortcuts"/>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Bookmark a page" id="bookmark-page">
        <procedure title="Bookmark the current page" id="add-bookmark" type="choices">
            <step>
                Click the bookmark button to the right of the address field.
                Its tooltip reads <control>Add to Bookmarks</control> or <control>Remove from Bookmarks</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Press <shortcut>Ctrl+D</shortcut>, or select <control>Add to Bookmarks</control> in the <control>More Options</control> menu.
            </step>
            <step>
                Right-click the page and select <control>Add to Bookmarks</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>GBrowser uses the page title as the bookmark name.</p>
        <p>
            To remove the bookmark, click the bookmark button again,
            or right-click its icon on the bookmarks bar and select <control>Remove Bookmark</control>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Use the bookmarks bar" id="bookmarks-bar">
        <p>
            The bookmarks bar under the address field shows one site icon for each bookmark.
            Hover over an icon to see the URL, and click it to open the page in the current tab.
        </p>
        <p>
            To remove a bookmark, right-click its icon and select <control>Remove Bookmark</control>.
        </p>
        <p>
            To hide the bar, clear <control>Show bookmarks toolbar</control> in
            <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic#toolwindow-settings">Tool Window Settings</a>.
        </p>
        <img src="gbrowser_bookmarks_bar.png" alt="GBrowser bookmarks bar under the address field with the Remove Bookmark menu open" width="620" border-effect="rounded"/>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Open a bookmark from the menu" id="bookmarks-menu">
        <procedure title="Open a saved bookmark" id="open-bookmark">
            <step>
                Click <control>More Options</control> at the right end of the browser toolbar.
            </step>
            <step>
                Select <control>Bookmarks</control> and then the bookmark.
                <img src="gbrowser_bookmarks_menu.png" alt="GBrowser More Options menu with the Bookmarks submenu listing saved bookmarks" width="590" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            If the current tab shows the home page, the bookmark opens in it.
            Otherwise, it opens in a new tab.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Edit bookmarks" id="edit-bookmarks">
        <procedure title="Rename, add or remove bookmarks" id="bookmark-manager">
            <p>The <control>Bookmark Manager</control> action is available when you have at least one bookmark.</p>
            <step>
                Press <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+B</shortcut>, or select <control>Bookmark Manager</control> in the <control>More Options</control> menu.
                The GBrowser settings open with the <control>Bookmark Management</control> group expanded.
            </step>
            <step>
                Make your changes in the bookmarks table:
                <list>
                    <li>To rename or change a bookmark, edit its <control>Name</control> or <control>URL</control> cell.</li>
                    <li>To add a bookmark, click the add button.</li>
                    <li>
                        To remove a bookmark, select it and click the remove button.
                        GBrowser deletes it right away, even if you then click <control>Cancel</control>.
                    </li>
                </list>
                <img src="gbrowser_settings_bookmarks.png" alt="Bookmark Management group in the GBrowser settings with a table of bookmark names and URLs" width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>OK</control>.
                A bookmark must have a URL; otherwise the dialog shows <control>URL cannot be empty</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Browsing history" id="history">
        <p>
            When <control>History enabled</control> is on, which is the default, GBrowser remembers the pages you visit.
            It keeps the 20 most recent pages by default; you can change the number, up to 60, in
            <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic#search-settings">Search Settings</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            GBrowser uses the history only for the suggestions in the address field.
            There is no separate history list.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Clear history and cookies" id="clear">
        <procedure title="Clear the browsing history" id="clear-history">
            <step>
                Click <control>More Options</control> and select <ui-path>Clear Cookies and History | Clear History</ui-path>,
                or press <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+7</shortcut>.
                <img src="gbrowser_clear_submenu.png" alt="GBrowser Clear Cookies and History submenu with the Clear Cookies and Clear History items" width="630" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>The action is available only when the history has entries.</p>

        <procedure title="Clear cookies" id="clear-cookies">
            <step>
                Click <control>More Options</control> and select <ui-path>Clear Cookies and History | Clear Cookies</ui-path>,
                or press <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+8</shortcut>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <warning>
            <control>Clear Cookies</control> deletes all cookies of the IDE's embedded Chromium browser without asking for confirmation.
            This signs you out of sites in GBrowser and can also affect other IDE features and plugins that show web pages.
        </warning>
    </chapter>

